484","lemma":"רַעְמָה","tr":"ra·mah","gloss":"Raamah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":159},{"base":"H2526","lemma":"חָם","tr":"cham","gloss":"Ham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H5210","lemma":"נִינְוֵה","tr":"nin·veh","gloss":"Nineveh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H6718","lemma":"צַ֫יִד","tr":"tsa·yid","gloss":"wild game","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":19},{"base":"H6721","lemma":"צִידוֹן","tr":"tsi·don","gloss":"Sidon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":496}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"That is why it is called Babel, for there the Lordconfused the language of the whole world, and from that place the Lordscattered them over the face of all the earth.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And as people journeyed eastward, they found a plain in the land of Shinar and settled there.","from":10},{"book":"JER","chapter":47,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For the day has come to destroy all the Philistines, to cut off from Tyre and Sidon every remaining ally. Indeed, the LORD is about to destroy the Philistines, the remnant from the coasts of Caphtor.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The name of the first river is Pishon; it winds through the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Nephilim were on the earth in those days—and afterward as well—when the sons of God had relations with the daughters of men. And they bore them children who became the mighty men of old, men of renown.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the earth was corrupt in the sight of God, and full of violence.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Ham, the father of Canaan, saw his fatherʼs nakedness and told his two brothers outside.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":1,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the whole world had one language and a common form of speech. And as people journeyed eastward, they found a plain in the land of Shinar and settled there. And they said to one another, “Come, let us make bricks and bake them thoroughly.” So they used brick instead of stone, and tar instead of mortar. “Come,” they said, “let us build for ourselves a city with a tower that reaches to the heavens, that we may make a name for ourselves and not be scattered over the face of all the earth.” Then the Lordcame down to see the city and the tower that the sons of men were building.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"21-32":{"people":[{"id":"eber-h5677g","name":"Eber","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shelah","count":3,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"shem-h8035","name":"Shem","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Noah","count":3,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"japheth-h3315","name":"Japheth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Noah","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"aram-h0758g","name":"Aram","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"arpachshad-h0775","name":"Arpachshad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"asshur-h0804h","name":"Asshur","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"elam-h5867c","name":"Elam","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"lud-h3865","name":"Lud","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shem","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"gether-h1666","name":"Gether","kind":"person","brief":"Early Patriarch","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"hul-h2343","name":"Hul","k